1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:05,417
AD 64. Rome burns. Nero plays the fiddle.

2
00:00:05,567 --> 00:00:08,617
Nope. Wrong instrument. Wrong place.

3
00:00:08,767 --> 00:00:10,817
Nero: the fiddling myth.

4
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:13,783
First: fiddles didn't exist yet.

5
00:00:13,933 --> 00:00:17,883
The violin came along 1,500 years later.

6
00:00:18,033 --> 00:00:20,383
Romans had the lyre.

7
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:23,550
Second: Nero wasn't even in Rome.

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:27,583
He was at his villa in Antium, miles away.

9
00:00:27,733 --> 00:00:30,083
When he heard, he rushed back.

10
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:33,383
He opened his gardens to the homeless.

11
00:00:33,533 --> 00:00:36,683
And brought in food from nearby towns.

12
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:39,317
So where did the music come from?

13
00:00:39,467 --> 00:00:41,517
It was a rumour.

14
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:46,383
People said he sang about the fall of Troy.

15
00:00:46,533 --> 00:00:50,217
Even the historian Tacitus called it a rumour.

16
00:00:50,367 --> 00:00:53,617
But Nero was unpopular. So it stuck.

17
00:00:53,767 --> 00:00:57,050
Was Nero a good emperor? Not really.

18
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,250
But he didn't fiddle.

19
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:02,483
Fiddles in ancient Rome: zero.

20
00:01:02,633 --> 00:01:05,817
Anyway, here's Nero fiddling.
